            <ArticleTitle>Paradoxical postural cerebrospinal fluid leak-induced headache: report of two cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>383-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jclinane.2008.01.011</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two patients with a history of dural puncture who developed paradoxical postural cerebrospinal fluid leak-induced headache. The patients' headache worsened when they were in the recumbent position, and it improved when they were placed upright. Both patients had a history of migraine headache. The patients were successfully treated with autologous epidural blood patch. The mechanism for PPCLH is to be elucidated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
